<metadata><name>Aneroid Lake Basin</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:359-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.267134" lon="-117.212596"><ele>1414.4</ele><name>End of the Wallowa Lake road</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:wallowa-lake-road-end (OSM gate node 14202499796, start of East Fork Wallowa Trail TR 1804); not moved; confidence: high; pdf_page: 361; book_elev_ft: 4646; quote: The end of the road at the south end of Wallowa Lake is the trailhead for the summer trail that leads to Aneroid Lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.208110" lon="-117.199160"><ele>2290.9</ele><name>Aneroid Lake (east shore)</name><desc>source: point on OSM East Fork Wallowa Trail TR 1804 east of Aneroid Lake (OSM way 305878747); DEM 7,516 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 362; book_elev_ft: 7520; quote: Aneroid Lake at 7,520 feet ... bypass the lake to the east, out of sight, to save time and to provide a direct route to Tenderfoot Basin</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.189900" lon="-117.205400"><ele>2585.1</ele><name>Tenderfoot Pass</name><desc>source: high point of OSM East Fork Wallowa Trail TR 1804 (way 305930762) south of the TR 1803 junction, DEM 8,481 ft; map 98 draws the ski route through Tenderfoot Pass; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 362; book_elev_ft: 8400; quote: Tenderfoot Basin, below the 8,400-foot pass of the same name ... 8 miles from the trailhead</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Aneroid Lake Basin</name><desc>1. End of the Wallowa Lake road -&gt; Aneroid Lake (east shore): osm (high), 6.14 mi | 2. Aneroid Lake (east shore) -&gt; Tenderfoot Pass: osm (medium), 2.03 mi</desc>
